{"type": "tool_call", "n": 61, "ts": 1790151516.739022, "tool": "flag_exception", "args": {"description": "JE-00300 \"Travel reimbursement - T. Vance\" ($6,300, posted 2026-03-29 by t.vance) has no supporting document attached and none could be located in the document store (searched \"T. Vance\", \"travel reimbursement\", \"expense report\" \u2014 no receipt/expense report found). Per Accounting Policy Manual (DOC-0005) \u00a72, an entry without support is not valid. This single entry accounts for ~99% of the $6,373 (811%) MoM increase in US Travel (6300), so the driver behind the Travel flux does not hold up until support is obtained (or the entry is reversed).", "amount": 6300, "related_ids": ["JE-00300"]}, "is_error": true, "result": {"error": "Tool-call budget of 60 exhausted. Call submit_memo now."}, "ms": 0}
{"type": "tool_call", "n": 62, "ts": 1790151532.509098, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US OPERATING EXPENSE FLUX \u2014 MARCH 2026 vs FEBRUARY 2026\n(Accounts 6000\u20137100, US entity, USD; period activity per GL)\n\nTotal operating expense: Feb $230,448.90 \u2192 Mar $254,514.90 (+$24,066.00, +10.4%)\n\nScreened every 6000\u20137100 line for >10% AND >$5,000 MoM movement. Two lines meet both thresholds:\n\n1) MARKETING PROGRAMS (6400): $7,898.14 \u2192 $29,686.00 (+$21,787.86, +275.9%) \u2014 MATERIAL, DRIVER HOLDS UP\n   Driven by two March AP invoices, both supported:\n   - JE-00241, 3/6/26, $22,000.00 \u2014 Meridian Events (Inv. ME-0588), Gold sponsorship for SaaS Connect Spring, event held 3/17\u20133/19/26. Support: DOC-0167. Invoice, sponsorship, and expense date all fall within March, so expensing in the period the event occurred is correct per policy (no prepaid issue since event \u22641 month out and within the same period).\n   - JE-00243, 3/6/26, $7,686.00 \u2014 Oakridge Creative (Inv. OAK-10546), content/campaign services for service period \"March 2026.\" Support: DOC-0168. Correctly expensed in the period of service.\n   February's balance was a single Oakridge Creative invoice (JE-00136, $7,898.14, DOC-supported) \u2014 a normal recurring retainer, so the February base is not itself an anomaly.\n   Conclusion: the $21.8K increase is a real, one-time sponsorship spend plus the normal content retainer \u2014 a legitimate, well-supported driver.\n\n2) TRAVEL (6300): $785.40 \u2192 $7,158.41 (+$6,373.01, +811.4%) \u2014 MATERIAL, DRIVER DOES NOT HOLD UP\n   March activity: normal card spend (Hilton $197.45, Delta $566.47, two Uber rides totaling $94.49 \u2014 all card-sourced, all with support) totaling ~$858, roughly in line with February's ~$785 of card travel spend (Uber, Delta, Hilton).\n   The variance is almost entirely one line: JE-00300, 3/29/26, $6,300.00, \"Travel reimbursement - T. Vance,\" a manual entry posted by t.vance (cash 1000 / Travel 6300), which represents 99% of the total Travel increase.\n   - This entry has NO supporting document attached (has_support=false), and I could not locate any receipt, expense report, or itemization for it in the document store despite searching \"T. Vance,\" \"travel reimbursement,\" and \"expense report.\"\n   - Per the Accounting Policy Manual (DOC-0005 \u00a72), \"every journal entry must have its supporting document(s) attached... an entry without support is not a valid entry.\"\n   - It is also worth noting the entry was self-posted by the same individual being reimbursed, which warrants controller attention independent of the support gap.\n   Conclusion: Excluding this unsupported $6,300 entry, underlying Travel spend is flat/normal MoM (~$858 vs ~$785, a routine variance well under both thresholds). The reported Travel flux driver does not hold up as currently documented.\n\nACTION NEEDED (not posted \u2014 could not attach support, per instructions):\n- I attempted to log a formal exception on JE-00300 ($6,300, unsupported travel reimbursement) via flag_exception but the call did not complete before this memo was due to a tool-call budget limit hit in this session. Please treat this memo as the exception flag: JE-00300 needs a receipt/expense report attached, or should be reversed, before the Travel line and total March opex can be considered clean. No entries were posted or reversed by me pending that documentation.\n\nAll other 6000\u20137100 lines (Salaries & Wages, Payroll Taxes, Rent, Utilities, Software Subscriptions, Meals & Entertainment, Training & Conferences, Office Supplies, Depreciation, Bank Fees, and all zero-activity accounts) moved less than $5,000 and/or less than 10% and are not flagged."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 8}
